[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42670"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/01940c9fa894d635300a49867da35d483b873a45d2a75204c20c58e4cb84c883.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. Given that $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s$, find $\\lambda $ and $\\mu .$" :question/worked-solution "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/a0d9fa1c366945e5e789b6361f929357af163db2e9be4a3ccc9023c12486aca6.png)\n\nIn $△ORT$ shown above, we have:\n\n- $OR=2|r|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{OR}$ has the opposite direction to $r$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{OR}=-2r.$\n\nSimilarly:\n\n- $RT=2|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-2s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =-2r-2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=-2r-2s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =-2$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-120268/selection/849f8ed38fc1a3de304df114133174791cd0c565eecdae331d7ca33d2bb616ce" :answer/id #uuid "905c6c4e-3fe6-5f97-a292-9c43daa5e840" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120268/selection/a9ff108d04c1e66a9f4c6f3310a9f0d04dc0e258e715199885db730e1e70d577" :answer/id #uuid "785a5215-204e-5370-b63f-8281b34f4e4b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-3$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120268/selection/8077f9e6d0361ea2e673595f8e74e40152bbcca2592ba3b3c731c521dbd536b7" :answer/id #uuid "dcb2d506-793c-5a3d-b8ac-0efc2d553542" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$\\lambda =2$ and $\\mu =-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120268/selection/07fc2b5749d4140e4451563688c