n\n- $RT=2|s|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ has the opposite direction to $s$\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{RT}=-2s.$\n\nAdditionally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t & =\\overset{\\to }{OR}+\\overset{\\to }{RT} \\\\  & =3r-2s.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $t=\\lambda r+\\mu s=3r-2s.$ \n\nSince $s∦r,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients, we get:\n\n- $\\lambda =3$ and $\\mu =-2$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120268/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45b6a076-8795-5510-aabc-62a925826dd0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120268"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-120303/selection/3b412da9b76f6a29030d56941e833d7d02d9e729f4421986ba782bd17b924be8" :answer/id #uuid "72a56613-fe00-52b3-b362-68b5b14d6ede" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{2}m+\\frac{1}{2}n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120303/selection/1b842a01aa096a343fb1d2039853b4c0b7134bae1d2ab28f39545e1b497a80c2" :answer/id #uuid "04f89674-d7af-5dc8-bfd9-2e087787aab9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{2}{3}m+\\frac{1}{3}n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120303/selection/6e86f9771603ec3deb36bcdbff2f982ab719be17ba3bc308225f2144e0b253c1" :answer/id #uuid "f98b29bb-af53-5033-85b6-2886693498ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{5}{9}m+\\frac{4}{9}n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120303/selection/ba2e613bb854c3c0affe9cc512ad8ffb580e67251431f1e4e680b917200ea27b" :answer/id #uuid "f1a1fce0-ac36-5b88-bd9c-087cb7e5f75e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{4}{9}m+\\frac{5}{9}n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120303/selection/a954a8974524117a7ab12453ab629e82ffaa3f2bd2168e08a12b2a7cc72747b8" :answer/id #uuid "5adaac84-a815-509a-81a5-14473e6256df" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\frac{1}{3}m+\\frac{2}{3}n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120303/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c63444f6-473b-524b-9370-90dd340d3013" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120303/selection/a954a8974524117a7ab12453ab629e82ffaa3f2bd2168e08a12b2a7cc72747b8" :answer-field/choices ["q-120303/selection/3b412da9b76f6a29030d56941e833d7d02d9e729f4421986ba782bd17b924be8" "q-120303/selection/1b842a01aa096a343fb1d2039853b4c0b7134bae1d2ab28f39545e1b497a80c2" "q-120303/selection/6e86f9771603ec3deb36bcdbff2f982ab719be17ba3bc308225f2144e0b253c1" "q-120303/selection/ba2e613bb854c3c0affe9cc512ad8ffb580e67251431f1e4e680b917200ea27b" "q-120303/selection/a954a8974524117a7ab12453ab629e82ffaa3f2bd2168e08a12b2a7cc72747b8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120303" :question/id #uuid "8b737947-533d-5a00-ac54-8d960f9a17b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-120303" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/50b87e86bd2985e54ce0a8fe6b3e23986f7e1946a5284d0ae297d96b9cbc60f6.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=m,$ $\\overset{\\to }{ON}=n$ and $P$ divides $\\overset{―}{MN}$ in the ratio $MP:PN=2:1.$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{OP}.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OP}=\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MP}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OM}=m,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{MP}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OMN,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{MN} & =\\overset{\\to }{MO}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{ON} \\\\  & =-m+n \\\\  & =n-m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $MP:PN=2:1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{MP}=\\frac{2}{3}\\overset{\\to }{MN}=\\frac{2}{3}(n-m).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OP} & =\\overset{\\to }{OM}+\\overset{\\to }{MP} \\\\  & =m+\\frac{2}{3}(n-m) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}m+\\frac{2}{3}n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-120303/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120303"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-322583/field-1/ada3e95027175c517d4a2506e551a1a45a5addd05dbd103451e7e1643b12efad" :answer/id #uuid "b24344f3-e43f-5877-8c52-00d67f759ded" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322583/field-1/074fc44ad49415c8e3a5af88be27e21a71cfc49cff2b8d2e55430066c784b9cc" :answer/id #uuid "04c500b4-bc8b-5a8e-a4f4-7be16f0e4ead" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322583/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "299eb5dc-e3f9-5f8f-b946-215414ec3411" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322583/field-1/ada3e95027175c517d4a2506e551a1a45a5addd05dbd103451e7e1643b12efad" :answer-field/choices ["q-322583/field-1/ada3e95027175c517d4a2506e551a1a45a5addd05dbd103451e7e1643b12efad" "q-322583/field-1/074fc44ad49415c8e3a5af88be27e21a71cfc49cff2b8d2e55430066c784b9cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322583/field-2/074fc44ad49415c8e3a5af88be27e21a71cfc49cff2b8d2e55430066c784b9cc" :answer/id #uuid "2b4298eb-febd-59a2-b671-7ff0e008f2dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-322583/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "381b66d8-b918-566b-bab4-e79f6eb429f5" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-322583/field-2/074fc44ad49415c8e3a5af88be27e21a71cfc49cff2b8d2e55430066c784b9cc" :answer-field/choices ["q-322583/field-2/074fc44ad49415c8e3a5af88be27e21a71cfc49cff2b8d2e55430066c784b9cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-322583" :question/id #uuid "35b7749d-a699-5471-bab4-16faa01f63ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-322583" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/d0e71a97dc559536c25b63fda50805875d4651166a9442ae0d3d081704edebb2.png)\n\nConsider the diagram above, where $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ $\\overset{\\to }{OQ}=q,$ and $N$ divides $\\overset{―}{AQ}$ in the ratio $AN:NQ=12:7.$ Express $\\overset{\\to }{ON}$ via the vectors $a$ and $q.$\n\n$\\,\\overset{\\to }{ON}=$\n{{field-1}}\n$a+$\n{{field-2}}\n$q$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{ON}=\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AN}.\n$$\n\nWe're told that $\\overset{\\to }{OA}=a,$ so we just need to work out $\\overset{\\to }{AN}.$\n\nFirst, from $△OAQ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AQ} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OQ} \\\\  & =-a+q \\\\  & =q-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $AN:NQ=12:7,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{AN}=\\frac{12}{19}\\overset{\\to }{AQ}=\\frac{12}{19}(q-a).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{ON} & =\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{AN} \\\\  & =a+\\frac{12}{19}(q-a) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{19}a+\\frac{12}{19}q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-322583/field-1" "q-322583/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "feae36e7-ae88-5f3a-957f-e65a92e399ad"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-322583"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-367064/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "c328b4b7-da8e-5a4f-ae5f-7584bce68984" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-367064/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "04f09979-820c-588c-a537-148693d26410" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-367064/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-367064/field-1/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-367064" :question/id #uuid "65028b3c-06a7-5ff4-b830-82c5ce361a6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-367064" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/80cedeceb8d377617af880cab1c383643e3cd79055eccce046b0418598897ac8.png)\n\nConsider the picture above. If $c=\\lambda a-2b,$ then$\\,\\lambda =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "To find $\\lambda ,$ we want to match the expression\n\n$$\nc=\\lambda a-2b.\n$$\n\nWe are given that one of the components is $-2b.$ So, we first draw the vector $-2b$ from the origin. Then we complete the path to the point $C.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14044176/assets/7e6923e8b8b774eeaa2f885ec6aa24bb03f07c547fa50e7145a4113a18e92e8a.png)\n\nLet $P$ be the endpoint of the vector $-2b.$ Then\n\n$$\nc=\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC}.\n$$\n\nIn $△OPC,$ we have:\n\n- $PC=2|a|$\n\n- $\\overset{\\to }{PC}$ and $a$ have opposite directions\n\nHence, $\\overset{\\to }{PC}=-2a.$\n\nAdditionally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =\\overset{\\to }{OP}+\\overset{\\to }{PC} \\\\  & =-2b-2a.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsequently, $c=\\lambda a-2b=-2a-2b.$\n\nSince $a∦b,$ the linear combination can only be written in one way. Equating the coefficients of $a,$ we get:\n\n$$\n\\lambda =-2\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-367064/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "58a49d00-cc58-5228-af38-9369cf31d8c8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-367064"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
